---
import HeroImage from '../../assets/project-zomboid-server-hero.png';
import Layout from '../../layouts/BlogPost.astro';

// Turnstile site key (public by design; the secret lives in the Worker).
const TURNSTILE_SITEKEY = '0x4AAAAAAF9DDEBz6_0wP2po';
const RUNBOOK = '/blog/project-zomboid-dedicated-server-ubuntu-26-04/';
---

<Layout
	title="Managed Project Zomboid Server for Modded Worlds — Peculiar Engineer"
	description="For private groups with a modded Project Zomboid world they'd hate to lose: game updates tested on a copy first, backups whose restores are actually tested, and rollback when an update or a mod goes wrong. Founding-customer price $25 a month, first month free."
	kind="page"
	showDate={false}
	heroImage={HeroImage}
>
	<p class="lede">
		Cheaper hosts give you a server, a control panel and a backup button. This is different: a person who looks
		after your group's world. Game updates get tested on a copy before they reach it, backups get restored
		to prove they work, and when an update or a mod goes wrong anyway, the world goes back to the last good backup.
	</p>
	<p>
		It's for a private group with an established, modded world that has been burned before: a mod update that
		broke the save, a game update that wouldn't load, progress lost to a backup that didn't restore. If you only
		need a server, a regular game host is cheaper, and that's the right choice.
	</p>

	<h2>What I do for your world</h2>
	<div class="table-wrap"><table>
		<thead>
			<tr><th>What usually goes wrong</th><th>What I do about it</th></tr>
		</thead>
		<tbody>
			<tr><td>A game update breaks the world</td><td>Tested on a copy of your world first, and applied only if it loads clean</td></tr>
			<tr><td>A game update goes wrong anyway</td><td>Snapshot before every update; rollback to the old build and the old world</td></tr>
			<tr><td>A Workshop mod update breaks the world</td><td>Mods update when the server restarts, so this can still happen. I roll back to the last backup (at most a day of progress) and hold the mod back</td></tr>
			<tr><td>A backup that won't restore</td><td>Daily off-server backups, and a test restore every month</td></tr>
			<tr><td>A bad mod hangs the server</td><td>Health check restarts it and alerts me; I pull the mod</td></tr>
			<tr><td>Crashes</td><td>Restarted automatically, back in a few minutes</td></tr>
			<tr><td>Admin chores</td><td>Whitelist, passwords, settings, resets: ask, and I do it</td></tr>
		</tbody>
	</table></div>

	<h2>Who it's for</h2>
	<ul>
		<li>Private groups of about 5 to 10 players, one world.</li>
		<li>Build 42, usually modded (a Workshop collection is ideal).</li>
		<li>Server in the US (East). Fine for North America; laggy from far away.</li>
	</ul>

	<h2>Price</h2>
	<p>
		<strong>$25 a month</strong> per group, a founding-customer price. The first month is free for the first
		couple of groups, in exchange for honest feedback. Cancel any time; if you leave, you get your world save.
	</p>

	<h2>The honest small print</h2>
	<ul>
		<li>
			It's one person, not a 24/7 support desk. The automation restarts crashed or hung servers and takes
			backups at 3 a.m.; a broken mod or anything else still needs me, when I'm awake.
		</li>
		<li>
			The server setup starts from <a href={RUNBOOK}>the public runbook</a>. Nothing is hidden, and you can always take
			it and run it yourself.
		</li>
		<li>
			Not affiliated with or endorsed by The Indie Stone. "Project Zomboid" is used only to say which game the
			server runs.
		</li>
	</ul>

	<h2 id="apply">Apply</h2>
	<p>Three questions. The rest can wait until we're talking.</p>
	<p class="form-error" id="form-error" role="alert" hidden></p>

	<form class="apply" method="post" action="/api/zomboid-apply">
		<label>Email <input name="email" type="email" required maxlength="254" autocomplete="email" /></label>
		<label>
			Group size
			<select name="group_size" required>
				<option value="">Choose…</option>
				<option value="2-4">2 to 4</option>
				<option value="5-8">5 to 8</option>
				<option value="9-10">9 to 10</option>
				<option value="11+">11 or more</option>
			</select>
		</label>
		<label>
			Workshop collection link (optional; leave blank for vanilla or if unsure)
			<input name="mods" type="text" maxlength="500" inputmode="url" placeholder="https://steamcommunity.com/sharedfiles/filedetails/?id=..." />
		</label>
		<div class="hp" aria-hidden="true">
			<label>Leave this empty <input name="website" tabindex="-1" autocomplete="off" /></label>
		</div>
		<div class="cf-turnstile" data-sitekey={TURNSTILE_SITEKEY} data-theme="dark"></div>
		<button type="submit">Apply</button>
		<p class="note">Your details are only used to reply to you; I don't share them. I reply by email within a couple of days.</p>
	</form>

	<script is:inline src="https://challenges.cloudflare.com/turnstile/v0/api.js" async defer></script>
	<script is:inline>
		(function () {
			var messages = {
				captcha: 'The spam check did not pass. Please try again.',
				invalid: 'Please check the email address and the group size, then send again.',
				server: 'Something broke on my side. Please try again in a few minutes.',
			};
			var code = new URLSearchParams(location.search).get('error');
			var box = document.getElementById('form-error');
			if (code && Object.prototype.hasOwnProperty.call(messages, code) && box) {
				box.textContent = messages[code];
				box.hidden = false;
			}
		})();
	</script>
</Layout>

<style>
	.lede {
		font-size: 1.1em;
	}
	form.apply {
		display: grid;
		gap: 1em;
		margin: 1.5em 0 2em;
	}
	form.apply label {
		display: grid;
		gap: 0.35em;
		font-family: var(--font-mono);
		font-size: 0.9rem;
		color: var(--sys-dim);
	}
	form.apply input,
	form.apply select,
	form.apply textarea {
		width: 100%;
		box-sizing: border-box;
		padding: 0.6em 0.7em;
		background: var(--sys-bg);
		color: var(--sys-text);
		border: 1px solid var(--sys-dim);
		border-radius: 4px;
		font: inherit;
		font-family: var(--font-mono);
		font-size: max(16px, 1em); /* under 16px, iOS Safari zooms on focus */
	}
	form.apply input:focus,
	form.apply select:focus,
	form.apply textarea:focus {
		outline: 2px solid var(--sys-fg);
		outline-offset: 1px;
	}
	form.apply button {
		justify-self: start;
		padding: 0.6em 1.6em;
		background: var(--sys-fg);
		color: var(--sys-bg);
		border: 0;
		border-radius: 4px;
		font-family: var(--font-mono);
		font-weight: 700;
		cursor: pointer;
	}
	form.apply .note {
		margin: 0;
		font-size: 0.85rem;
		color: var(--sys-dim);
	}
	.hp {
		position: absolute;
		left: -10000px;
		width: 1px;
		height: 1px;
		overflow: hidden;
	}
	.form-error {
		padding: 0.8em 1em;
		border: 1px solid #ff5f56;
		color: #ff9f99;
		font-family: var(--font-mono);
		font-size: 0.9rem;
	}
</style>
